      "start_seconds": 0.88,
      "end_seconds": 8.22,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second. Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.19,
      "end_seconds": 15.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "doctor, it's nausea. It's getting on my nerves now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.41,
      "end_seconds": 18.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.43,
      "end_seconds": 28.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "let me think, you know, I'd say one week actually, no, closer to two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.03,
      "end_seconds": 29.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.33,
      "end_seconds": 36.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "I've been feeling weak too, you know, for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.84,
      "end_seconds": 40.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.98,
      "end_seconds": 44.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "it feels moderate to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.91,
      "end_seconds": 50.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Yes. And what about blood in the stool, weight loss or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.01,
      "end_seconds": 58.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "I haven't had blood in the stool, weight loss or rash, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.98,
      "end_seconds": 62.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.57,
      "end_seconds": 67.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "No, um, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.58,
      "end_seconds": 71.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.88,
      "end_seconds": 75.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.81,
      "end_seconds": 79.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.54,
      "end_seconds": 86.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.41,
      "end_seconds": 90.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.05,
      "end_seconds": 93.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I'm on glibenclamide, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.61,
      "end_seconds": 97.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.33,
      "end_seconds": 100.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.0,
      "end_seconds": 106.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.47,
      "end_seconds": 112.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.01,
      "end_seconds": 117.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.51,
      "end_seconds": 121.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "my mother had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.56,
      "end_seconds": 133.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.27,
      "end_seconds": 138.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.05,
      "end_seconds": 146.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.02,
      "end_seconds": 151.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.84,
      "end_seconds": 154.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.36,
      "end_seconds": 160.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.9,
      "end_seconds": 181.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.59,
      "end_seconds": 193.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "okay, this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.24,
      "end_seconds": 217.47,
      "duration_seconds": 14.23,
      "text": "Okay: BMI works out to 26.0, temperature is 39.0 degrees. And height 172 centimetres, heart rate 97, saturation 96 percent, weight 77 kilos, blood pressure 113 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.83,
      "end_seconds": 221.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.92,
      "end_seconds": 234.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "yes, that's fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.55,
      "end_seconds": 237.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.75,
      "end_seconds": 251.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "You're mildly dehydrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.21,
      "end_seconds": 256.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "so, good, you can sit up again"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.22,
      "end_seconds": 275.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I'd lean towards acute gastroenteritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.73,
      "end_seconds": 279.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Is this serious, uh, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.27,
      "end_seconds": 317.18,
      "duration_seconds": 31.91,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with acute gastroenteritis do well once it's treated properly. Let's book blood salts to look into dehydration. I'm going to put you on ORS, 1 sachet, after each loose stool, for three days. That's for dehydration. Stick to bananas, rice, toast, curd, and avoid milk and oily food till it settles. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.91,
      "end_seconds": 321.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    }
  ]
